 "about": "Each house front's picture read as bays and storey bands (px in its 1024-px picture, y down): bays [x0, x1] pier middle to pier middle, one window column each, 'door' where the ground floor has the front's door; bands: the rows a wall is built from (ground at the street, mid repeated for a taller house, top with the cornice); windows: the glass of every window [x0, y0, x1, y1], for the rooms seen through them (interiors.js). Read by eye from the pictures, 9 Nov 2026. 'hood': what the picture paints over the door, to be built out from the wall (js/world/facaderelief.js): kind 'gable' (x0, x1 its eaves' ends, cx, y0 its top, ye the eaves, y1 its underside) or 'flat' (the box x0, y0, x1, y1), depth in m, brackets [x0, x1, to y], cols [x0, x1, y0, y1, m proud], wall [x0, y0, x1, y1] plain wall to cover the painted one; 'trim': a window casing's px at the sides, over the head and under the sill.",
